+    The forward path does ``torch.cat(self.pooler_output, dim=0)`` AND (for
+    Qwen3-VL) reads ``self.deepstack_features`` — a list of per-level (Nrows, D)
+    tensors whose row count MUST equal the (compressed) pooler row count, see
+    modeling_qwen3_vl.py:L1306 + _deepstack_process L941. So we expose BOTH:
+    ``pooler_output`` = list of compressed (Nq_i, D) per video block, and
+    ``deepstack_features`` = list (one per deepstack level) of the same blocks'
+    deepstack rows pruned with the SAME kept indices. For Qwen2.5-VL (no
+    deepstack) we set ``deepstack_features=None`` and the LM forward ignores it.
     """
-    def __init__(self, t):
+    def __init__(self, t, deepstack_features=None):
         self.pooler_output = t
+        self.deepstack_features = deepstack_features


